#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:2
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr "术语表"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:4
msgid ""
"This page includes a number of terms that we use in our documentation, so "
"that you have a reference for how we're using them."
msgstr "本页收录了我们在文档中使用的若干术语，供你查阅我们使用它们的方式。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:8
msgid "CI/CD"
msgstr "CI/CD"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:10
msgid ""
"CI/CD is a common way to write *Continuous Integration and Continuous "
"Deployment*. In some scenarios, they exist as two separate platforms. Read "
"the Docs is a combined CI/CD platform made for documentation."
msgstr ""
"CI/CD 是 *持续集成与持续部署* （Continuous Integration and Continuous "
"Deployment）的常见写法。在某些场景下，二者是两个相互独立的平台。Read the Docs 则是一个面向文档的 CI/CD 一体化平台。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:13
msgid "configuration file"
msgstr "配置文件"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:15
msgid ""
"YAML configuration file (e.g. ``.readthedocs.yaml``) that configures the "
"build process of your project on Read the Docs."
msgstr "用于配置你的项目在 Read the Docs 上构建过程的 YAML 配置文件（例如 ``.readthedocs.yaml`` ）。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:19
msgid ":doc:`/config-file/index`"
msgstr ":doc:`/config-file/index`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:20
msgid "Practical steps to add a configuration file to your documentation project."
msgstr "为文档项目添加配置文件的实操步骤。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:22
msgid "dashboard"
msgstr "仪表盘"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:24
msgid ""
"The \"admin\" site where Read the Docs projects are managed and configured. "
"This varies for our two properties:"
msgstr "对 Read the Docs 项目进行管理和配置的“管理”站点。我们的两个站点在这方面有所不同："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:27
msgid "|com_brand|: https://app.readthedocs.com/dashboard/"
msgstr "|com_brand|：https://app.readthedocs.com/dashboard/"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:28
msgid "|org_brand|: https://app.readthedocs.org/dashboard/"
msgstr "|org_brand|：https://app.readthedocs.org/dashboard/"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:29
msgid "default version"
msgstr "默认版本"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:31
msgid ""
"Projects have a *default version*, usually the latest stable version of a "
"project. The *default version* is the URL that is redirected to when a users"
" loads the `/` URL for your project."
msgstr "每个项目都有一个*默认版本* ，通常是项目最新的稳定版本。当用户访问你项目的 `/` URL 时，重定向的目标即为*默认版本* 的 URL。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:33
msgid "diff"
msgstr "diff"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:35
msgid ""
"A way to see the changes between two pieces of text, which shows the added "
"and removed content with a green and red color respectively."
msgstr "一种查看两段文本之间差异的方式，以绿色和红色分别显示新增与删除的内容。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:37
msgid "discoverability"
msgstr "可发现性"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:39
msgid ""
"A documentation page is said to be *discoverable* when a user that needs it "
"can find it through various methods: Navigation, search, and links from "
"other pages are the most typical ways of making content *discoverable*."
msgstr "当需要某个文档页面的用户能够通过多种途径找到它时，该页面即具有*可发现性* ：导航、搜索以及来自其他页面的链接，是让内容具有*可发现性* 的最典型方式。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:41
msgid "Docs as Code"
msgstr "Docs as Code"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:43
msgid ""
"A term used to describe the workflow of keeping documentation in a Git "
"repository, along with source code. Popular in the open source software "
"movement, and used by many technology companies."
msgstr "用于描述“将文档与源代码一同保存在 Git 仓库中”这一工作流的术语。它在开源软件运动中颇为流行，也被许多科技公司采用。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:47
msgid "flyout menu"
msgstr "浮出菜单"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:49
msgid ""
"Menu displayed on the documentation, readily accessible for readers, "
"containing the list active versions, links to static downloads, and other "
"useful links. Read more in our :doc:`/flyout-menu` page."
msgstr ""
"显示在文档页面上、便于读者随时访问的菜单，其中包含活跃版本列表、静态下载链接以及其他实用链接。更多信息见我们的 :doc:`/flyout-menu` "
"页面。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:51
msgid "GitOps"
msgstr "GitOps"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:53
msgid ""
"Denotes the use of code maintained in Git to automate building, testing, and"
" deployment of infrastructure. In terms of documentation, GitOps is "
"applicable for Read the Docs, as the configuration for building "
"documentation is stored in ``.readthedocs.yaml``, and rules for publication "
"of documentation can be :doc:`automated </automation-rules>`. Similar to "
":term:`Docs as Code`."
msgstr ""
"指使用保存在 Git 中的代码来自动化基础设施的构建、测试与部署。就文档而言，GitOps 同样适用于 Read the Docs：构建文档的配置存储在"
" ``.readthedocs.yaml`` 中，而文档的发布规则可以 :doc:`自动化 </automation-rules>` 。类似于 "
":term:`Docs as Code` 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:59
msgid "maintainer"
msgstr "维护者"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:61
msgid ""
"A *maintainer* is a special role that only exists on |org_brand|. The "
"creator of a project on |org_brand| can invite other collaborators as "
"*maintainers* with full ownership rights."
msgstr "*维护者* 是仅存在于 |org_brand| 的特殊角色。|org_brand| 上项目的创建者可以邀请其他协作者成为拥有完整所有权的*维护者* 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:64
msgid ""
"The *maintainer* role does not exist on |com_brand|, which instead provides "
":doc:`/commercial/organizations`."
msgstr "*维护者* 角色在 |com_brand| 上不存在，取而代之的是 :doc:`/commercial/organizations` 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:65
msgid "pinning"
msgstr "固定"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:67
msgid ""
"To *pin* a requirement means to explicitly specify which version should be "
"used. *Pinning* software requirements is the most important technique to "
"make a project :term:`reproducible`."
msgstr "*固定* （pin）某个依赖意味着显式指定应使用的版本。*固定* 软件依赖是让项目 :term:`可复现 <reproducible>` 的最重要技术。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:70
msgid ""
"When documentation builds, software dependencies are installed in their "
"latest versions permitted by the pinning specification. Since software "
"packages are frequently released, we are usually trying to avoid "
"incompatibilities in a new release from suddenly breaking a documentation "
"build."
msgstr "文档构建时，软件依赖会按固定规范所允许的最新版本安装。由于软件包发布频繁，我们通常要避免新版本中的不兼容问题突然破坏文档构建。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:75
msgid "Examples of Python dependencies::"
msgstr "Python 依赖示例::"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:86
msgid "Read the Docs recommends using **exact pinning**."
msgstr "Read the Docs 建议使用**精确固定** 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:88
#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:112
msgid "See: :doc:`/guides/reproducible-builds`."
msgstr "参见：:doc:`/guides/reproducible-builds` 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:89
msgid "pre-defined build jobs"
msgstr "预定义构建作业"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:91
msgid ""
"Commands executed by Read the Docs when performing the build process. They "
"cannot be overwritten by the user."
msgstr "Read the Docs 在执行构建过程时运行的命令。用户无法覆盖它们。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:93
msgid "project home"
msgstr "项目主页"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:95
msgid ""
"Page where you can access all the features of Read the Docs, from having an "
"overview to browsing the latest builds or administering your project."
msgstr "你可以在此页面访问 Read the Docs 的全部功能：纵览项目概况、浏览最新构建或管理你的项目。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:97
msgid "project page"
msgstr "项目页面"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:99
msgid "Another name for :term:`project home`."
msgstr ":term:`project home` 的别称。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:100
msgid "reproducible"
msgstr "可复现"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:102
msgid ""
"A documentation project is said to be *reproducible* when its sources build "
"correctly on Read the Docs over a period of many years. You can also think "
"of being *reproducible* as being *robust* or *resillient*."
msgstr "当文档项目的源码多年来在 Read the Docs 上持续正确构建时，即可称其是*可复现* 的。你也可以把*可复现* 理解为*健壮* 或*有韧性* 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:105
msgid ""
"Being \"reproducible\" is an important positive quality goal of "
"documentation."
msgstr "“可复现”是文档质量的一个重要正面目标。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:107
msgid ""
"When builds are not reproducible and break due to external factors, they "
"need frequent troubleshooting and manual fixing."
msgstr "当构建不可复现、因外部因素而损坏时，就需要频繁排查并手动修复。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:110
msgid ""
"The most common external factor is that new versions of software "
"dependencies are released."
msgstr "最常见的外部因素是软件依赖发布了新版本。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:113
msgid "root URL"
msgstr "根 URL"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:115
msgid ""
"Home URL of your documentation without the ``/<lang>`` and ``/<version>`` "
"segments. For projects without custom domains, the one ending in "
"``.readthedocs.io/`` (for example, ``https://docs.readthedocs.io`` as "
"opposed to ``https://docs.readthedocs.io/en/latest``)."
msgstr ""
"文档的主 URL，不含 ``/<lang>`` 与 ``/<version>`` 段。对于没有自定义域名的项目，即以 "
"``.readthedocs.io/`` 结尾的 URL（例如 ``https://docs.readthedocs.io`` ，而非 "
"``https://docs.readthedocs.io/en/latest`` ）。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:118
msgid "slug"
msgstr "slug"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:120
msgid ""
"A unique identifier for a project or version. This value comes from the "
"project or version name, which is reduced to lowercase letters, numbers, and"
" hyphens. You can retrieve your project or version slugs from :doc:`our API "
"<api/v3>`."
msgstr ""
"项目或版本的唯一标识符。该值来自项目或版本的名称，会被缩减为小写字母、数字和连字符。你可以从 :doc:`我们的 API <api/v3>` "
"获取项目或版本的 slug。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:124
msgid "static website"
msgstr "静态网站"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:126
msgid ""
"A static site or static website is a collection of HTML files, images, CSS "
"and JavaScript that are served statically, as opposed to dynamic websites "
"that generate a unique response for each request, using databases and user "
"sessions."
msgstr ""
"静态站点或静态网站是以静态方式提供的 HTML 文件、图片、CSS 和 JavaScript "
"的集合；与之相对，动态网站则借助数据库和用户会话为每个请求生成唯一的响应。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:129
msgid ""
"Static websites are highly portable, as they do not depend on the webserver."
" They can also be viewed offline."
msgstr "静态网站的可移植性很高，因为它们不依赖于 Web 服务器，还可以离线查看。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:132
msgid "Documentation projects served on Read the Docs are *static websites*."
msgstr "在 Read the Docs 上提供的文档项目都是*静态网站* 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:134
msgid ""
"Tools to manage and generate static websites are commonly known as *static "
"site generators* and there is a big overlap with documentation tools. Some "
"static site generators are also documentation tools, and some documentation "
"tools are also used to generate normal websites."
msgstr "管理和生成静态网站的工具通常被称为*静态站点生成器* ，它们与文档工具有很大重叠。有些静态站点生成器同时也是文档工具，而有些文档工具也被用于生成普通网站。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:138
msgid ""
"For instance, :doc:`Sphinx <sphinx:index>` is made for documentation but "
"also used for blogging."
msgstr "例如，:doc:`Sphinx <sphinx:index>` 为文档而生，但也可用于写博客。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:139
msgid "subproject"
msgstr "子项目"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:141
msgid ""
"Project A can be configured such that when requesting a URL ``/projects"
"/<subproject-slug>``, the root of project B is returned. In this case, "
"*project B* is the subproject. Read more in :doc:`/subprojects`."
msgstr ""
"可以对项目 A 进行配置，使得请求 URL ``/projects/<subproject-slug>`` 时返回项目 B 的根路径。此时，*项目 B*"
" 就是子项目。更多信息见 :doc:`/subprojects` 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:145
msgid "user-defined build jobs"
msgstr "用户自定义构建作业"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:147
msgid ""
"Commands defined by the user that Read the Docs will execute when performing"
" the build process."
msgstr "由用户定义、Read the Docs 将在执行构建过程时运行的命令。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:148
msgid "virtualenv"
msgstr "virtualenv"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:150
msgid ""
"The default way for Python projects to create an isolated environment. This "
"ensures that a :doc:`reproducible set of dependencies </guides/reproducible-"
"builds>` are installed so that you project builds the same way each time."
msgstr ""
"Python 项目创建隔离环境的默认方式。它确保安装一组 :doc:`可复现的依赖 </guides/reproducible-builds>` "
"，使你的项目每次都以相同方式构建。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:151
msgid "webhook"
msgstr "webhook"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:153
msgid ""
"A webhook is a special URL that can be called from another service, usually "
"with a secret token. It is commonly used to start a build or a deployment or"
" to send a status update."
msgstr "webhook 是一种可由其他服务调用的特殊 URL，通常带有私密令牌。它常用于启动构建或部署，或发送状态更新。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:157
msgid "There are two important types of webhooks for Read the Docs:"
msgstr "对 Read the Docs 而言，有两类重要的 webhook："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:159
msgid ""
"Git providers have webhooks which are special URLs that Read the Docs can "
"call in order to notify about documentation builds."
msgstr "Git 提供方拥有 webhook——即 Read the Docs 可调用以获知文档构建通知的特殊 URL。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:160
msgid ""
"Read the Docs has a unique webhook for each project that the Git provider "
"calls when changes happen in Git."
msgstr "Read the Docs 为每个项目提供一个唯一的 webhook，当 Git 中发生变更时，Git 提供方会调用它。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:164
msgid ":doc:`/guides/setup/git-repo-manual`"
msgstr ":doc:`/guides/setup/git-repo-manual`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:165
msgid "Manually configuration for Git repositories."
msgstr "手动配置 Git 仓库。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:167
msgid ":doc:`/build-notifications`"
msgstr ":doc:`/build-notifications`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/glossary.rst:168
msgid "Receive notifications when your documentation builds fail."
msgstr "在文档构建失败时接收通知。"

